{"verdict":"changes_requested","issues":[{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":0,"description":"The prescribed root cause fix requires ContentstackProvider to subscribe to Stack live preview callbacks (e.g. Stack.onEntryChange) to update the content value in context, replacing the static useMemo over defaultContent. Per learned review rules from prior investigation, the implementation hand-rolls a raw window.addEventListener('message', ...) listener with a fragile extractDraftContent function that guesses at payload shape (payload?.data?.entry ?? payload?.entry ?? payload?.content ?? payload?.data?.content) instead of using the Contentstack SDK's documented onEntryChange/onLivePreview callback API. This does not use the SDK's documented API and is likely to break when the SDK changes its message format. The prescribed root cause fix is not correctly implemented at the context/provider level.","suggestedFix":"Remove the hand-rolled window.addEventListener('message', ...) listener and extractDraftContent function. Instead, subscribe to the Contentstack SDK's documented live preview callback (Stack.onEntryChange or Stack.onLivePreview) inside ContentstackProvider's useEffect, and call setContent with the updated entry data from the SDK callback. This is the SDK's supported entry point for receiving draft content updates."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":0,"description":"extractDraftContent uses untyped 'any' (Record<string, any>) without an explanatory comment, violating TypeScript strict compliance. The function also unsafely casts arbitrary JSON to Partial<IContentstackContext> without validation.","suggestedFix":"If any intermediate type is genuinely unavoidable, add an explanatory comment per project TypeScript strict compliance rules. Better yet, remove extractDraftContent entirely and use the SDK's typed callback, which returns properly typed entry objects."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"test/unit/","line":0,"description":"No unit tests exist for this change. No test files matching 'contentstack', 'livepreview', or 'preview' were found beyond the pre-existing src/services/__tests__/contentstack.spec.ts. The acceptance criteria require verification of: draft vs published content rendering on GO/UP/MX sites, successive edits, multi-instance updates, connection-loss resilience, and entry switching — none of these are covered by tests. The total test count is not increased by this change.","suggestedFix":"Add vitest unit tests in test/unit/ mirroring the src/ path structure. Tests should cover: (1) ContentstackProvider subscribing to SDK live preview callbacks and updating context content, (2) useContent returning updated draft content after an onEntryChange event, (3) fallback to last valid content when draft contains empty/invalid fields, (4) cleanup of event listeners on unmount."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":17,"description":"CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST and CONTENTSTACK_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN are destructured from process.env but there is no validation or warning when live preview is expected but these values are missing. If CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST is empty, live_preview is silently omitted from options, making it difficult to diagnose why live preview doesn't work.","suggestedFix":"Add a logger.warn() when CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST is empty but live preview is expected (e.g. when a CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLED env var is true), similar to the existing validation pattern for other required env vars."}],"summary":"The implementation partially addresses the prescribed root cause: src/services/contentstack.ts correctly adds the live_preview configuration (enable: true, host, management_token) to the Stack options, which is the first half of the prescribed fix. However, the second half — subscribing to the SDK's onEntryChange callback in ContentstackContext to update context content — appears to be replaced with a hand-rolled window.addEventListener('message', ...) listener and a fragile extractDraftContent function that guesses at payload shape instead of using the SDK's documented API. This violates the prescribed minimal fix, TypeScript strict compliance (untyped any without comments, unsafe casts), and the concision/reuse requirement (the SDK already provides the callback mechanism). Additionally, no unit tests were added for any of the live preview functionality, failing the test coverage requirement. Verdict: changes_requested with 3 blockers and 1 major issue."}
